      "code_snippet": "On ProMotion iPhones, third-party animations are capped at 60fps unless `CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone` is set. Recent Expo SDKs set it by default — confirm it's there, and add it if not:\n\n```json\n{ \"expo\": { \"ios\": { \"infoPlist\": { \"CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone\": true } } } }\n```\n\nThen the frame budget is 8ms, not 16. This is also why a UI-thread animation matters more on mobile than it does on web.",
